    description: "WI-lubap (dev 2e9611808f) made the subprocess->CLI linker argparse-aware (add_parser/set_defaults -> handler join). Fire was explicitly deferred: fire.Fire(obj) exposes obj's METHODS as subcommands reflectively — there is no add_parser/set_defaults idiom to scan, so the subcommand->handler mapping must be derived from the class/dict passed to fire.Fire() (its public methods become subcommands, method name = subcommand name). Scope: detect fire.Fire(<name>) calls, resolve <name> to a class/module symbol, and register its public methods as subcommand->handler entries in the subprocess linker's command_by_name (mirroring _scan_argparse_commands). Lower priority than argparse (fire is rarer). Behavioral close-check: a subprocess.run(['tool','method']) against a fire.Fire(Cls) whose Cls has a method 'method' emits a subprocess_calls edge to Cls.method."  # 1500
    fields: {}  # 1500
