- op: discuss  # d757
  at: '2026-07-04T13:50:48Z'  # d757
  by: agent  # d757
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d757
  clock: 3  # d757
  nonce: d757  # d757
  message: "LANDED — PR merged, dev e3dc463098. The subprocess->CLI linker now joins subprocess.run(['tool','method']) to the public methods of a class exposed via fire.Fire(<Class>), mirroring the WI-lubap argparse pattern (_scan_fire_commands + _fire_target_name). The fire map shares command_by_name (inherits the INV-zuhub multi-candidate fallback; coexists with argparse + concept=command) and is counted by the requirement diagnostic.\n\nAdversarial review (4 refuters) returned GO_WITH_FIXES; the one MAJOR (D1) was an INV-fahub over-join: name-only class matching harvested methods of ANY class named <target> repo-wide, so a method unique to a never-fired same-named class became the SOLE candidate -> a confidently-wrong 0.85 edge (the INV-zuhub fallback only catches multi-candidate collisions; live repro confirmed). FIXED structurally: a fire target now resolves ONLY to a kind=class Symbol DEFINED IN the same file as the fire.Fire() call ((rel_path, name) match), so a same-named class in another module is never harvested. Added a regression test (two same-name Calc classes in different files -> the never-fired one's method does not join). Minor fixes: docstring now documents the func-shape deferrals + instance form; count test tightened to ==1; positive test asserts confidence==0.85.\n\nAdditive only (new subprocess_calls edges to existing method symbols; taint- and coherence-neutral). Deferred forms (module/instance/dict target, a class IMPORTED from another module, bare 'from fire import Fire') fail SAFE to no join. Behavioral (end-to-end): fire.Fire(Calc) with add/multiply/_private + subprocess.run(['tool','add']/['tool','multiply']) -> subprocess_calls to Calc.add + Calc.multiply; _private never exposed. 100% cov; smart-test 3931 passed."  # d757
